{"id": "2026-08-05-news-russian-barrage-kills-17-in-kyiv", "date": "2026-08-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "Russian barrage kills 17 in Kyiv", "summary": "A Russian overnight missile-and-drone barrage on Kyiv killed at least 17, nearly double a 1 August strike, as Ukraine cited its interceptor shortage.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/8/5/russian-attacks-kill-17-exploiting-ukraines-lack-of-missile-interceptors", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Ukraine's State Emergency Service said cleanup operations were under way after what it called a \"massive attack\"; President Volodymyr Zelensky said Russia had fired 29 missiles and 115 drones, and again argued that lives could have been saved had allies replenished Ukraine's stock of interceptors — the surface-to-air missiles (chiefly US-made Patriots) that shoot down incoming ballistic weapons — none of which the defence managed to bring down. Warehouse facilities in Brovary, on Kyiv's eastern edge, were among the sites hit. Moscow described the salvo as \"precision\" strikes on military targets, a characterisation Ukrainian authorities — reporting civilian deaths and damaged civilian infrastructure — reject.", "why": "the interceptor shortage Zelensky keeps naming is becoming the war's decisive variable, turning each unreplenished air-defence battery directly into civilian deaths when the next salvo comes — and it lands as Kyiv's Western backers weigh how fast they can resupply.", "thread_id": "2026-08-01-news-russian-missiles-kill-nine-in-kyiv", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-01", "event_date": "2026-08-05", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Russia", "Ukraine", "Kyiv", "Volodymyr Zelensky"]}
{"id": "2026-08-05-news-us-iran-oman-near-hormuz-deal", "date": "2026-08-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "US, Iran, Oman near Hormuz deal", "summary": "US Treasury chief Bessent said a US-Iran-Oman interim deal to reopen the Strait of Hormuz could come within a day, per Axios, though no text is confirmed.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/international/nahost/krieg-im-nahen-osten-deal-zu-hormus-laut-axios-in-reichweite", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The strait, the Gulf chokepoint south of Iran through which roughly a quarter of the world's seaborne oil and a large share of its liquefied-natural-gas and fertiliser trade passes, has been squeezed by months of tit-for-tat since the late-February military escalation between Washington and Tehran. A fresh analysis published by the International Trade Centre (the joint WTO-UNCTAD trade agency) found LNG shipments through the strait have fallen by about 95%, with higher insurance and freight costs rippling well beyond the region. Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian said Iran was defending its borders and did not intend to widen the conflict, while President Trump publicly warned Iran would be hit \"very hard\" absent an opening. No text has been published and the parties have not jointly confirmed terms, so the \"within reach\" framing rests on Bessent's account of the negotiations.", "why": "a reopening would ease a real global squeeze on oil and fertiliser shipping — but the gap between Bessent's optimism and the absence of any signed, published deal is the part to watch, given how often ceasefire-adjacent claims in this conflict have not held.", "thread_id": "2026-08-05-news-us-iran-oman-near-hormuz-deal", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-05", "event_date": "2026-08-05", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["United States", "Iran", "Oman", "Strait of Hormuz"]}
{"id": "2026-08-05-news-us-revokes-brazil-ambassador-s-visa", "date": "2026-08-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "US revokes Brazil ambassador's visa", "summary": "Washington revoked the visa of Brazil's US ambassador in retaliation for Brasilia not approving Trump's ambassador nominee, escalating a feud weeks before Brazil's election.", "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/04/us-revokes-brazil-ambassador-visa", "source_domain": "theguardian.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The department framed the move as retaliation for Brasilia's refusal to approve Trump's nominee for ambassador in Brazil — Daniel Perez, a Florida Republican and ally of Secretary of State Marco Rubio — and for Brazil's decision last month to deny visas to two US diplomats seeking to visit ahead of the October election. Viotti, a former senior UN official, has not been expelled, but the department said that if she left the country she would have to reapply for a visa, and warned of further action if Brasilia keeps withholding approval; it called the step \"a reciprocal action\" and said Brazil had \"continually delayed and obfuscated.\" Those are the administration's characterisations — Brasilia has cast the earlier visa denials as a defence of its election against foreign interference. The dispute is entangled with Brazil's bitter campaign, in which Lula, 80, seeks a fourth term against Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, a Trump ally.", "why": "it pulls a G20 democracy's ambassador into a personal-appointments standoff weeks before a national vote, and signals Washington is willing to use visa tools as leverage in a contested foreign election.", "thread_id": "2026-07-26-news-brazil-denies-visas-to-us-envoys", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-26", "event_date": "2026-08-04", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["United States", "Brazil", "Lula", "Marco Rubio"]}
{"id": "2026-08-05-news-guatemala-s-fuego-volcano-erupts", "date": "2026-08-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "Guatemala's Fuego volcano erupts", "summary": "Guatemala's Fuego volcano erupted and intensified, sending ash 6km high and forcing hundreds — reportedly up to 1,700 — to evacuate under the second-highest alert.", "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/04/guatemala-volcano-eruption-prompts-evacuation-of-hundreds-of-people", "source_domain": "theguardian.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Firefighters evacuated at least 350 residents of the villages of El Porvenir and Las Lajitas to the municipality of San Juan Alotenango, with authorities reporting far larger numbers moved as the eruption grew — Al Jazeera put the figure around 1,700. The 3,763-metre volcano sits less than 100 kilometres from Guatemala City; residents described leaving of their own accord in fear as rivers of lava tumbled down the mountainside. It was a 2018 eruption of the same volcano that killed hundreds in nearby communities, which is why authorities move quickly on evacuations here.", "why": "Fuego's proximity to densely populated valleys makes even a moderate eruption a mass-displacement event, and the speed of the evacuation reflects hard lessons from the deadly 2018 disaster.", "thread_id": "2026-08-05-news-guatemala-s-fuego-volcano-erupts", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-05", "event_date": "2026-08-03", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Guatemala", "Fuego volcano"]}
{"id": "2026-08-05-news-wfp-warns-el-nino-to-deepen-hunger", "date": "2026-08-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "WFP warns El Nino to deepen hunger", "summary": "The UN World Food Programme forecast a strengthening El Nino could push about 50 million more people into acute hunger across 45 countries into 2027.", "url": "https://www.wfp.org/news/world-food-programme-ramps-preparedness-and-response-plans-el-nino-threatens-push-tens", "source_domain": "wfp.org", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["new source"], "topics": ["world", "health"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "El Nino — a recurring warming of the tropical Pacific that shifts rainfall patterns worldwide every few years — is shaping up, forecasters say, to be the strongest in at least 70 years; the WFP's analysis (issued from Rome) singles out Central and South America, the Caribbean and southern Africa as likely worst hit, with reduced rainfall also threatening harvests across south and south-east Asia. The agency said it is ramping up preparedness and pre-positioning aid, warning that impacts are already reaching the most vulnerable. One WFP expert cautioned the biggest southern-African blow may not land until the 2027-28 lean season.", "why": "this is a forecast, not a tally, but it quantifies how a natural climate cycle — amplified by background warming — is set to compound conflict- and price-driven hunger, and it lands as humanitarian budgets are already stretched thin.", "thread_id": "2026-08-05-news-wfp-warns-el-nino-to-deepen-hunger", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-05", "event_date": "2026-08-05", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["WFP", "El Nino"]}
{"id": "2026-08-05-news-glencore-posts-4-4bn-half-year-profit", "date": "2026-08-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "Glencore posts $4.4bn half-year profit", "summary": "Zug-based Glencore reported a $4.4bn first-half 2026 profit after two loss-making halves, with revenue up nearly 50% to $174.4bn.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/wirtschaft/rohstoffkonzern-glencore-mit-hohem-gewinn-nach-auf-und-ab-bei-energiepreisen", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["economy", "switzerland"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Revenue climbed almost 50% to $174.4 billion, which the company attributed to firmer commodity prices and volatile energy markets that its trading arm was positioned to exploit. The rebound reverses a rough stretch for the Baar-based firm, whose earnings track closely with global metal and fuel prices.", "why": "Glencore is one of the largest companies domiciled in Switzerland and a bellwether for global commodity demand, so a swing of this size signals both firmer raw-material markets and a recovery in one of the Swiss economy's heavyweight employers and taxpayers.", "thread_id": "2026-08-05-news-glencore-posts-4-4bn-half-year-profit", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-05", "event_date": "2026-08-05", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Glencore"]}
{"id": "2026-08-05-news-infantino-holds-fifa-crisis-meeting", "date": "2026-08-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "Infantino holds FIFA crisis meeting", "summary": "FIFA's Infantino called a crisis meeting amid an extortion allegation after his failed bid to sell off World Cup commercial rights.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/international/kritik-an-fifa-reisst-nicht-ab-erpressungsvorwuerfe-gegen-infantino-krisensitzung-einberufen", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The head of Jordan's football association, Prince Ali bin al-Hussein, wrote on X that FIFA had withheld payments due to his federation and that he was told during the last World Cup it \"would help\" his association if he backed Infantino — conduct he characterised as amounting to extortion, which he said he refused to accept. Al-Hussein, a former FIFA vice-president, ran unsuccessfully against Infantino for the presidency in 2016. The world football body, legally domiciled in Zurich, has faced mounting criticism since the aborted rights sell-off.", "why": "governance turmoil at a Zurich-based world federation revives long-running scrutiny of FIFA's accountability from its Swiss home — and the allegation, so far one official's public account, is the kind that has repeatedly dogged the organisation.", "thread_id": "2026-08-05-news-infantino-holds-fifa-crisis-meeting", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-05", "event_date": "2026-08-05", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["FIFA", "Gianni Infantino"]}
{"id": "2026-08-05-news-gotthard-road-tunnel-shut-12-nights", "date": "2026-08-05", "stream": "news", "headline": "Gotthard road tunnel shut 12 nights", "summary": "The Gotthard road tunnel will close for 12 nights from 10 to 27 August for maintenance, diverting southbound Ticino traffic over the pass.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/suisse/le-tunnel-routier-du-gothard-sera-ferme-durant-douze-nuits", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "During the night closures, drivers heading south to Ticino will have to cross over the Gotthard pass instead; the daytime tunnel remains open.", "why": "the Gotthard is Switzerland's principal Alpine road artery, and even partial night closures in the summer holiday season reroute cross-country and transit traffic onto the slower, weather-exposed mountain pass.", "thread_id": "2026-08-05-news-gotthard-road-tunnel-shut-12-nights", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-05", "event_date": "2026-08-10", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Gotthard Tunnel", "Ticino"]}
